      <div type="clause" n="69.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 69.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hwa æfter ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.1"/> wite crafige, beo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.11"/> he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.1"/> his weres scyldig wið þone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.12"/> cingc.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf hwá æfter ðam wite crauian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.2"/>, beo he his weres scyldig wið ðone cyningc.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hwa æfter wite crafige, be his weres scyldig wið þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.3"/> cyningc.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.6"/> si quis forisfacturam inde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.7"/> crauabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.8"/>, wérę suę reus sit erga regem.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi aliquis dehinc forisfacturam aliquam exegerit ab aliquo, qui eos adiuuare ad hoc noluerit, pretium suum, id est þere, regi persoluat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi quis ab eo forisfacturam exegerit, redempcionis sue reus sit erga regem.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="69.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="208" ed="#robertson"/>And gyf hwá æfter ðam<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_69-2.robnote.fn.4"/> wite crauian [wille]<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_69-2.robnote.fn.9"/>, beo he his weres scyldig wið ðone cyningc.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="288" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gif hwa æfter ðam wite crafige, beo he his weres scyldig wið þone cingc.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn nach diesem [Zeitpunkt] éiner [der Vögte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.de.1"/> für Gastung] Strafgeld einfordert<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_69-2.lnote.de.2"/>, sei er sein Wergeld schuldig gegenüber dem König.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if after this [time] anyone [of the reeves] demands a fine [for hospitality], let him be liable for his wergild to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_69-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="209" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone [of my reeves] shall demand<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_69-2.robnote.n.2"/> a fine [in such a case], he shall forfeit his wergeld to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone after this demands a fine, he is to forfeit his wergild to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="289" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if any of my reeves solicits a bribe, his wergild shall be forfeit to the king.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 357, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ðam: omitted A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">exig. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">exig. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> wille? <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 30,6 <hi rend="italic">Hs. A; halbe Zeile frei</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply wille? cf. 30,6 MS A; half a line left blank</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cr. i. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cr. i. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">grau. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">grau. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">be <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">be Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðonne cyninge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðonne cyninge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 63</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">see above 63</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Lateiner verstehen ‘Strafgeld bei Weigerung der Gastungsbeihilfe für den Vogt’. Allein <hi rend="italic">wite</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Wb</hi> 3a. 4) hat hier den allgemeineren Sinn: ‘Abgabe, Gebühr’; <hi rend="italic">vgl. biscopwite</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The Latin translators understand ‘a fine for refusing the contribution to the reeve’s hospitality’. But <hi rend="italic">wite</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> 3a. 4) has here the more general sense ‘due, fee’; <hi rend="italic">cf. biscopwite</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_69-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">crafian</hi> ist Lehnwort aus Nordischem; <hi rend="italic">cravare</hi> im Anglolatein häufig; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>. Strafe auch ähnlicher Fälle ist Wergeld; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 30e. f. g</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">crafian</hi> is a loan-word from Norse; <hi rend="italic">cravare</hi> is frequent in Anglo-Latin; <hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>. The penalty in similar cases too is wergild; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 30e. f. g</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_69-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The reference is doubtless to the last few words of the preceding clause. The case suggested is that of a reeve who tries to treat the voluntary payment there mentioned as a compulsory tax.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_69-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">crafian</hi> is a Scandinavian loan word.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_69-2.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><label>hwæt</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_69-2.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><label>wille</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. B; <hi rend="italic">crafige</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
